    m_MinSize: 3
    m_MaxSize: 300
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "DelayedActions works perfectly with <b>recursive</b> functions. \nLets
    say you want to do to something every 3 seconds, use DelayedActions in the way
    shown in this section's code.\n\n<b>What happens to delayed actions when the
    game ends, the scene changes or the gameobject is destroyed? </b> \nDelayedActions
    will automatically abort all actions of that executor, so you dont have to worry
    about it. \n\n<i><b>WARNING</b></i>: that won't happen for a <i>disabled</i>
    state, call DelayedActions.Abort(this) OnDisable if you want it to stop in that
    case"
