    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'DA works by default under the <i>DelayedActions</i> tag.

    You can
    organize your actions by <b>tags</b> using <b>classes</b> names.

    Each tag
    will trigger the creation of a new group, a new gameobject which executes the
    actions. This doesn''t have any effect on the execution of actions.


    <b>How
    do I use/create tags?</b>

    To use DA with a tag just call DelayedActions<T>.Do(...)
    where T is a class. T can be <b>any</b> class: yours, Unity''s or even a private
    empty class.

    You can also create a ''shortcut'' for your tag by using DA''s
    inheritance.

    In this section''s sample code you''ll see examples of how
    to use it.

'
