    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "<b>How do I cancel (abort) an action already scheduled?</b>\nFirst you
    need to know that each action has an ID (automatic) and a locator (given by you
    default 0).\nAlso, each action will be under an executor (mandatory) and inside
    a group (Tags, not using tags is default).\n\nYou can:\n\t\tAbort a whole group:
    \"DelayedActions<MyTag>.AbortGroup();\"  Destroys the group's gameObject aswell.\n\n\t\tAbort
    an executor: \"DelayedActions.Abort(this);\" Every action under said executor
    is aborted.\n\n\t\tAbort an action of an executor: \"DelayedActions.Abort(locator,
    this);\" If more than one action share locator all of them are aborted, use this
    to your advantage.\n\n\t\tAbort by locator: \"DelayedActions.Abort(locator);\"
    Regardelss of executor.\n\t\t\n\t\tAbort by ID. Only one action will be affected
    (IDs are unique)\n\nNote: IDs, locators and executors of different groups are
    dependant (calling abort of any kind will never abort other groups' actions)."
